  "findings": [
    "Prepared rows still replay all selected raw spikes; this is the structural latency cost.",
    "Sparse NumPy counting improves the regular fixture from7.2s to3.0s and Poisson-like fixture from7.08s to4.54s.",
    "Naive scalar Numba fusion and forced helper inlining do not accelerate these cases; no10x claim is established.",
    "Prepared exact likely-pair results can eliminate query replay for those exact memberships. Arbitrary multiway merges and threshold descendants require additional evidence or exact fallback.",
    "Global interaction sparsity must not be assumed from selected-root sparsity.",
    "Selective page authentication/time directories and certified independent partitions enable sparse access and bounded parallel processing.",
    "Numba/hybrid, multicore and GPU options require measured end-to-end wins including authentication, startup/JIT and memory."
  ],
